WEBVTT

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.758
["Don't Wanna Go Home"
by Tom Waits playing]

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.436
♪ Oh, darling ♪

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:22.522
♪ Since we met ♪

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:25.442
♪ I can't sleep... ♪

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:29.112
[mom] I would like to see my son
be happy and settled down.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.781
He's had two really close relationships,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.910
so I think he's scared to put his heart
back out there for it to be broken again.

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:37.746
Hey, how's it going?

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:42.834
♪ And I don't wanna go home... ♪

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.461
[man] I've known Brandon
for a few years now,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.713
and I think he's so focused

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:49.132
on looking for the right guy

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.135
that he misses the great guys
that are right in front of him.

00:00:58.516 --> 00:01:01.770
He is sarcastic
and he will poke fun at you,

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:05.523
but he's also probably
the nicest person that I've met,

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:09.903
and I don't know that he has found a match
yet that can complement him in both ways.

00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:12.155
[song continues]

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:23.416
[mom] It's been very hard for him to

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.753
find the right one,
but I'm sure he's out there somewhere.

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:28.922
Hopefully he'll find true love soon.

00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:32.092
Hi.

00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:41.226
[Justin] Hey.

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:43.144
Are you my date?

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:45.188
[chuckles] I am. I'm Justin.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.481
Justin, nice to meet you.

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:47.774
-Nice to meet you.
-How are you?

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:48.733
I'm good.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:50.151
You have a nice little smile.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:51.236
I like this color.

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:52.779
Thank you. I like this jacket.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:53.863
That's a good jacket.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.865
You know,
it's a little somethin'-somethin'.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.450
-[chuckles]
-You want to go inside?

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.827
-Yeah, let's do it.
-All right.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.203
How are you feeling?

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.246
I'm good, how are you?

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:04.207
I'm a little nervous. It feels...
But it's a good nervous, you know?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.208
It'll be nice.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.836
I'm excited, you know,
to get to know you more.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.295
[Justin] Yeah. Into it.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:11.464
Yeah? Let's see
what else you're into, then.

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:12.966
[both chuckling]

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:20.723
So nice in here.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.642
It is so nice in here.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.436
[grunts] I like your little purse.
Or is it a clutch?

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.313
I would say it's a clutch. [laughs]

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:28.731
I always gotta have a clutch.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.859
[laughs] What do you have in here?

00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:32.152
-Good evening.
-Hey!

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:33.778
-[bartender] How you doing?
-Good.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:35.280
-What do you wanna drink?
-I love your hair.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:37.907
-[bartender] Thank you.
-I'm gonna do a dirty, dirty martini.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.450
-Dirty, dirty.
-With vermouth.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:40.869
-You like it dirty?
-I do. [laughs]

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:42.996
Your drinks... Just your drinks?

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:44.247
-Just my drinks.
-Okay.

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:56.551
Hi. [laughs]

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:57.594
How are you doing?

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.596
Hi, how are you?

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.055
-I'm good.
-You're so handsome.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.223
-Thank you.
-Hi, Ronald.

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:04.309
-Hi, Brandon.
-You look so cute.

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:05.602
Yeah, I dressed myself.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.978
-It's kind of a thing.
-Finally?

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:08.730
Yeah, you know,
Mom stopped doing it for me.

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:11.566
-You finally moved out of the house?
-Okay, I will fight you.

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:13.151
-How've you been?
-Doing good.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.277
-How are you?
-I'm good.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.278
What's new?

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:16.779
This.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.657
-This? Yeah.
-This is nice. Yeah. I like this. [laughs]

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:22.076
[Brandon] I remember the first time
meeting you,

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.245
-and I remember how handsome you were.
-[Ronald] We met, like...

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:25.538
This'll be the third Mardi Gras,

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:27.040
-but it was two Mardi Gras ago.
-Two Mardi Gras ago.

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:29.125
I'm so glad it's you. I'm happy.

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.043
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:31.544
-Good.
-You look handsome.

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:33.213
-I try.
-I like this.

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:35.381
Have you been here before?

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.466
A couple of times?

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.675
I heard it's haunted.

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:39.093
-Is it?
-That's what I heard.

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.304
-Okay. It'll be fine.
-Somebody got murdered upstairs.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.723
If I go to the bathroom
and don't come back, you'll know why.

00:03:43.806 --> 00:03:45.558
I figure you just would have left.

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.101
[both laughing]

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.269
[Brandon] You got nice eyes.

00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:50.647
-[laughs]
-Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.898
[Brandon] Yeah, okay.

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:52.815
Yeah.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:53.858
Yeah.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.902
-[Andrew] Are you from New Orleans?
-I am.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:56.861
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.945 --> 00:03:59.072
-Born and raised. What about you?
-I'm not from here.

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:01.616
I, uh... Born in Upstate New York
but grew up in Ohio...

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:03.326
-Okay.
-...and kind of a military brat,

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.410
moved around a bit.

00:04:04.494 --> 00:04:05.703
I'm from Memphis originally.

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:07.497
-Memphis? Okay.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.957
When did you move to New Orleans?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.918
Initially, the end of 1998.

00:04:12.126 --> 00:04:13.086
It's been a while.

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:15.088
I actually came here
to visit some friends...

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:17.048
-Okay.
-...and I kind of caught the bug.

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:19.384
I also had, like, gone to a crawfish boil.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.095
You know? And I got some of those
authentic New Orleans experiences

00:04:22.178 --> 00:04:23.054
that, like--

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:24.305
Do you eat crawfish?

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:25.223
Oh, I eat crawfish.

00:04:25.306 --> 00:04:27.141
Do you know how to eat them properly?

00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:29.227
-I was taught by a Cajun.
-Okay.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.520
AKA, my ex-boyfriend.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.688
-Oh, okay.
-Who,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.981
like, taught me the proper way,

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:35.275
and to suck the heads
and all of that, so...

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:36.234
[laughs]

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:38.361
All right. Then he taught you well.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.779
I think he did, I think he did.

00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:41.572
Probably more than you need to.

00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:42.699
Yeah, probably so.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.659
-It's good to know. Um...
-Yeah.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.578
Are you involved in anything, like,

00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:49.789
outside of, like, what you do?

00:04:49.872 --> 00:04:52.166
-Yeah.
-I haven't asked you that. What do you do?

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.418
Let's go there first.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.545
So I'm the creative director at an agency.

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:57.088
-Nice, okay.
-Yep.

00:04:57.171 --> 00:04:59.632
Uh, it's a whole bunch of, like,
running around,

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:03.136
kind of being stressed out,
and then trying to get shit done.

00:05:03.219 --> 00:05:04.095
[chuckles]

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:06.889
So I'm doing hair.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.017
Nice. I can tell, it looks really good.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.977
Thanks. Almost ten years.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:11.894
It's not moving.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.438
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

00:05:13.521 --> 00:05:15.940
-You can help me with mine.
-No [laughs]

00:05:16.024 --> 00:05:18.067
-Wait, what do you do?
-Uh, I'm a teacher.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.027
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.403
-Okay.
-I love it.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.863
-What grade?
-Kindergarten.

00:05:22.405 --> 00:05:23.656
-What?
-[laughs]

00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:25.199
That's fun.

00:05:25.283 --> 00:05:27.160
-You like kids?
-So I'm also a creative director

00:05:27.243 --> 00:05:28.369
of kids.

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.246
I'm running around
like I'm stressed out, too.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.123
You know, we're creating stuff.

00:05:32.206 --> 00:05:33.249
[laughs]

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:34.459
You must love kids.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:35.626
-I do.
-That's awesome.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.794
-What about you?
-I love kids.

00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:39.047
You get to be someone's hero all the time,

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.131
-you know?
-Right.

00:05:40.214 --> 00:05:41.507
I feel like kids need a champion,

00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:43.426
and you get to be that person,
which is cool.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.552
-[Jonathan L.] Wow.
-Yeah.

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:46.471
Oh, my gosh, I love it.

00:05:46.554 --> 00:05:47.972
Well, what are you looking for?

00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:50.558
I mean, everybody's looking
for the same thing, right?

00:05:50.641 --> 00:05:51.851
-I don't think so.
-Really?

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.270
No, I've met some people
who are not looking for that.

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.438
[both laughing]

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.273
-You'd be surprised.
-Okay, okay.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:58.775
I feel like...

00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:01.986
ultimately, I'm looking to find a partner.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.988
-Okay.
-Like, I want...

00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:06.657
uh, somebody that I'll be with
for a long time.

00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:08.576
-Okay. That's awesome.
-What about you?

00:06:08.659 --> 00:06:10.036
-Same.
-Okay.

00:06:10.119 --> 00:06:12.371
I guess now I'm in the stage of my life
where it's like,

00:06:12.455 --> 00:06:14.290
-I want that next step, too.
-Okay.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.208
Yeah.

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:18.086
-There's alignment there, I guess.
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:19.045
[laughs]

00:06:19.754 --> 00:06:21.047
[chuckles]

00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:23.299
I don't know if you remember
my Tinder profile.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:25.051
I don't know, I swiped left.

00:06:25.134 --> 00:06:27.011
No, you swiped right, 'cause we matched,

00:06:27.095 --> 00:06:28.763
and we messaged, so don't... [chuckles]

00:06:28.846 --> 00:06:31.057
Don't play, 'cause I can
pull up the receipts now if I need to.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:34.060
Um, but that was also three years ago,

00:06:34.143 --> 00:06:35.645
so you might not remember.
Dementia sets in.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:36.854
[gasps]

00:06:36.938 --> 00:06:38.648
Close your mouth. Close your mouth.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:39.690
[chuckles]

00:06:40.316 --> 00:06:41.567
Do you like blue cheese olives?

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.862
-[clears throat]
-[laughs]

00:06:44.946 --> 00:06:46.781
[exhales, clears throat]
Does that answer your question?

00:06:46.864 --> 00:06:48.616
Olives? You don't like olives?

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:49.659
I love an olive.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.911
There's something with
a blue cheese olive...

00:06:51.994 --> 00:06:52.995
-Really?
-Blue cheese... Yeah.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.456
I mean, and to each his own,
like, that...

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.582
makes you happy.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.753
Um, do you want to continue
this conversation at the table?

00:07:00.837 --> 00:07:01.671
I do.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.673
But I'm going to eat
my blue cheese olive first.

00:07:05.049 --> 00:07:06.801
-[laughs]
-Okay, let's go.

00:07:06.884 --> 00:07:07.927
Ugh, gross.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.637
It's so good.

00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:11.305
That was your last one.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:14.016
Please don't order
anything blue cheese tonight.

00:07:22.066 --> 00:07:23.234
[Brandon] Are you hungry?

00:07:23.317 --> 00:07:25.570
I am kind of hungry. Are you hungry?

00:07:25.653 --> 00:07:27.071
-I'm starving.
-[chuckles]

00:07:27.155 --> 00:07:29.532
I mean, I won't say starving,
but definitely hungry.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.284
-I heard the food's really good here.
-Yeah?

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.202
I heard good things.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.789
-Take your little shawl off.
-[laughs]

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:39.041
Now, you know, like, I'm almost jealous,

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:42.962
or, like, wish I had enough confidence,
like, to be this.

00:07:43.754 --> 00:07:45.506
It's like, how does this happen?

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.717
It's taken me a long time to

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.511
-be comfortable in my own skin.
-'Kay.

00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.763
But now I'm just kind of like,

00:07:52.847 --> 00:07:55.641
I wear what I want to wear,
I want to do what I want to do.

00:07:55.725 --> 00:07:58.144
And then if that person comes along

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:02.148
that wants to be... have
the Jonathan experience, then great.

00:08:02.231 --> 00:08:05.193
But if they don't, then their loss.

00:08:05.276 --> 00:08:06.903
-The Jonathan experience?
-[chuckles]

00:08:07.028 --> 00:08:09.405
Let's rewind and elaborate.
What is the Jonathan experience?

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.990
Do you have your own website?

00:08:11.073 --> 00:08:13.951
-Is this like a catering company?
-No, just this. The Jonathan experience.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.954
[both laughing]

00:08:17.038 --> 00:08:18.164
[Brandon] What's your story?

00:08:18.915 --> 00:08:19.957
[Justin] Uh...

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:23.044
So, yeah, I grew up
in a single-parent household.

00:08:23.127 --> 00:08:26.130
Mom, uh, kicked ass and...

00:08:26.214 --> 00:08:27.548
-I can tell.
-[laughs]

00:08:27.632 --> 00:08:29.258
She did a really damn good job.

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.510
I'll have to thank her.

00:08:31.052 --> 00:08:33.930
Um... [laughing]

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.892
[chuckles]

00:08:38.226 --> 00:08:40.394
[waiter] Hello, there.
I'll be your server this evening.

00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:41.562
Amazing. Thank you.

00:08:41.646 --> 00:08:43.606
-How are you?
-[waiter] Fantastic, thank you.

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.858
-There's some water for you.
-Thank you.

00:08:45.942 --> 00:08:47.401
Do you know what you want, Ronald?

00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:50.154
Um, can I do the shrimp cocktail?

00:08:50.238 --> 00:08:51.781
Can we share that,
or do you want to get two?

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:53.658
-Absolutely, we could share.
-Okay, let's share that.

00:08:53.741 --> 00:08:56.244
-Yes.
-Um, and then for dinner,

00:08:56.744 --> 00:08:58.871
I'm gonna go with the iceberg wedge salad

00:08:58.955 --> 00:09:01.165
with the grilled shrimp,
and no blue cheese, please.

00:09:01.249 --> 00:09:05.336
Um, I'm going to do
the iceberg wedge salad...

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:07.380
-Okay.
-...with blue cheese.

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:09.966
-[grunts]
-[chuckles]

00:09:10.132 --> 00:09:11.884
I had really big ears as a kid.

00:09:11.968 --> 00:09:13.886
-[Justin] Uh-huh.
-Like, my head was really small.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:14.887
[Justin laughs]

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.932
-So all you'd see walking down...
-[laughs]

00:09:18.015 --> 00:09:20.893
All you saw walking down the street
was these big satellites.

00:09:20.977 --> 00:09:22.979
It was like, I had every...

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.939
Everything in the book
they would tell me, like,

00:09:25.022 --> 00:09:27.358
-"You catch satellite HBO?"
-Oh, no!

00:09:27.441 --> 00:09:29.277
They would call me Dumbo, and...

00:09:29.777 --> 00:09:31.153
I remember going home crying,

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.781
and my dad would be like,
"It's okay, it's okay."

00:09:34.365 --> 00:09:35.241
He's like, "Son,

00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:38.202
if anyone tells you have Dumbo ears,
just say,

00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:41.706
'You know, I may be Dumbo,
but I'm packing a jumbo.'"

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:44.041
[both laughing]

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.003
-Come on, Dad.
-I swear to God. I'm like,

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:49.005
"I don't think
you should be telling me this.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:50.089
I'm 12."

00:09:50.172 --> 00:09:51.757
[laughs]

00:09:51.841 --> 00:09:55.428
If it was, um... the right situation,
I absolutely would love to have kids.

00:09:55.511 --> 00:09:57.513
-Yeah.
-I want the whole package.

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:59.598
I want what...
You know, my parents had that.

00:09:59.682 --> 00:10:03.561
My parents were... My stepmom and my dad
were married for 35 years,

00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:05.438
and I see that that could...
It's possible.

00:10:05.521 --> 00:10:06.647
-I feel the same way.
-Yeah.

00:10:06.731 --> 00:10:08.524
-Obviously, I love kids. Um...
-Yeah.

00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:10.943
But again, you need
that person in your life

00:10:11.027 --> 00:10:12.945
who wants to go to that next level.

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:16.365
I want to be wholeheartedly committed
to someone,

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:19.452
or a group of people. [chuckles]
Um...

00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:21.537
Are you into, like, thruples,

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:23.581
-open relationships?
-I don't know. Never done it.

00:10:23.664 --> 00:10:25.374
But would I be open to doing it?
Absolutely.

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.001
-Okay. All right.
-Absolutely.

00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:32.214
So it's important for me to be with
somebody that can express themselves...

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:35.760
-Mm-hmm.
-...and have an opinion about things,

00:10:36.052 --> 00:10:38.763
and, like, be passionate about anything.

00:10:39.347 --> 00:10:41.390
Like, whether it's teaching children...

00:10:42.058 --> 00:10:44.018
[chuckles] or whether it's...

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:48.397
Whatever it is, I want somebody
to have that kind of fire

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:51.108
and that passion, or, like,
know where they stand.

00:10:51.525 --> 00:10:54.236
Why do you think you're still single?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.656
I think that a lot of people,
 they get base level Ronald,

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.117
but until I'm very comfortable
in a situation,

00:11:00.201 --> 00:11:01.285
you're not gonna get, like--

00:11:01.369 --> 00:11:02.828
Why do people get base-level Ronald?

00:11:02.912 --> 00:11:04.538
I always feel like
I get base-level Ronald.

00:11:04.622 --> 00:11:06.457
Why-- Why would I share

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.543
more than base-level Ronald with you
until I get to know you?

00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:12.546
-That's how you build relationships--
-That's also how you get hurt.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.048
But what's wrong with getting hurt?

00:11:14.131 --> 00:11:16.634
What's wrong with getting hurt?
A lot of things.

00:11:16.717 --> 00:11:20.304
I know, but I feel like we build as people
when we get hurt sometimes.

00:11:20.388 --> 00:11:22.973
I agree. I wholeheartedly agree. However,

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:24.058
I also...

00:11:24.141 --> 00:11:27.269
The person that I am is not
going to feel comfortable sharing

00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.480
with someone until they get to that level.

00:11:29.563 --> 00:11:32.191
How long do I have to be in your life
before you get to that level?

00:11:32.274 --> 00:11:33.693
-Well, who knows?
-Fifteen, 20?

00:11:33.776 --> 00:11:36.320
Brandon, you could be in my life
for two more days and get to that level,

00:11:36.404 --> 00:11:37.947
the way you're pushing.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.365
I mean, that's why I'm pushing.

00:11:39.448 --> 00:11:40.616
I mean, maybe.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.661
How was your meal?

00:11:44.161 --> 00:11:45.162
It was really good.

00:11:45.246 --> 00:11:47.039
-Mine was good, too.
-I enjoyed it.

00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:49.542
Yeah? You want to go get a drink
somewhere else?

00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:50.709
Yeah, I'd like that.

00:11:50.793 --> 00:11:52.795
Yeah? Me too.

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:54.672
-Ready?
-Yeah, let's do it.

00:12:10.354 --> 00:12:12.648
-[Jonathan L.] Can I smoke a cigarette?
-[Brandon groans]

00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:14.316
I know. I'm sorry.

00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:17.278
-It's like one of my...
-[laughs]

00:12:17.361 --> 00:12:18.654
I mean, it's not a pet peeve.

00:12:18.738 --> 00:12:20.865
I mean, you got to do you,
but, yeah, go ahead.

00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:24.285
It's not like my hugest...

00:12:24.493 --> 00:12:26.412
-Turn-offs?
-You do you, it's fine.

00:12:26.495 --> 00:12:28.747
Yeah, it's one of my turn-offs,
but that's you, right?

00:12:28.831 --> 00:12:31.500
-Mm-hmm.
-You gotta make yourself happy.

00:12:31.834 --> 00:12:34.420
-That's your, like, after-dinner mint?
-Mm-hmm.

00:12:34.503 --> 00:12:35.629
Smoking a cigarette?

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.883
-I know. I know.
-It's kind of a deal-breaker,

00:12:38.966 --> 00:12:41.343
'cause, like, I'm not, like,
really attracted to it.

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:44.346
So no cigarettes, no blue cheese.

00:12:46.515 --> 00:12:47.516
[Brandon] Any pets?

00:12:47.892 --> 00:12:49.852
[Justin] So, pets, I love pets.

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:51.270
-[Brandon] Do you have any?
-[Justin] No.

00:12:51.353 --> 00:12:53.564
-Unfortunately not. No.
-Do you have a plant?

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:56.108
So, my plant, Edgar,

00:12:56.358 --> 00:12:58.277
-I kept him alive...
-Hold... Whoa, whoa.

00:12:58.819 --> 00:13:02.239
First of all, you named the plant.
Go ahead, go ahead, I'm listening.

00:13:02.323 --> 00:13:03.199
So...

00:13:03.991 --> 00:13:06.952
I kept Edgar alive
for about a year and a half.

00:13:07.036 --> 00:13:09.455
What was Edgar before he died, evidently?

00:13:09.538 --> 00:13:10.790
I don't know what he was.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:12.458
[chuckles]

00:13:12.541 --> 00:13:15.294
Was he, like, a tree? Was he a flower?

00:13:16.545 --> 00:13:17.546
You have no idea?

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.758
It was just, like, a little plant.
[chuckles]

00:13:21.425 --> 00:13:23.135
-Obviously I feel like--
-I definitely agree.

00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:24.678
-I'm very attracted to you.
-I agree.

00:13:24.762 --> 00:13:26.430
And it's just like, hmm...

00:13:27.848 --> 00:13:29.266
What do we do about it?

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:30.601
[Ronald] What's holding it back?

00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:32.728
Yeah, that, too. What's holding it back?

00:13:32.812 --> 00:13:34.772
Honestly, I feel like
it's New Orleans in general,

00:13:34.855 --> 00:13:38.067
because I feel like if you make
one wrong turn or one wrong move,

00:13:38.442 --> 00:13:41.695
your entire social life,
your entire life in general,

00:13:41.779 --> 00:13:44.782
just blows up, because everybody is
in everybody's business.

00:13:44.865 --> 00:13:46.283
I get that, but, like...

00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:49.662
I mean, we're not talking about
dating the entire city.

00:13:49.745 --> 00:13:52.373
We're just talking about,
you know, two people.

00:13:52.456 --> 00:13:54.875
-You and me?
-Yeah, you know, I mean...

00:13:54.959 --> 00:13:55.834
You know?

00:13:58.379 --> 00:14:02.424
Um, yeah, I mean, I think
you're a great guy and all, I just

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:04.385
kind of feel like
we're on different pages.

00:14:04.468 --> 00:14:05.928
-Yeah.
-Or want different things,

00:14:06.011 --> 00:14:08.973
but I really, like, enjoyed
this experience, and, like...

00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:11.517
-Me, too.
-I had a good time, and I feel like

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.143
maybe I'll bring some cheetah out

00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:14.353
-into my life next time.
-Yes!

00:14:14.436 --> 00:14:18.148
You definitely brought
that little spice out, that little sass.

00:14:18.232 --> 00:14:20.192
-[laughs]
-Like, I appreciate, like...

00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:22.152
I appreciate it. I appreciate you.

00:14:22.236 --> 00:14:23.737
-I appreciate you.
-All right.

00:14:23.821 --> 00:14:24.697
Thank you.

00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:26.657
-Bye.
-Let's get you inside.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:27.616
Okay.

00:14:27.825 --> 00:14:29.243
Be careful heading home.

00:14:29.326 --> 00:14:32.204
-Oh, I will.
-Don't stop at any stranger's house.

00:14:32.288 --> 00:14:34.582
[laughs]

00:14:34.748 --> 00:14:35.583
Bye.

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:46.010
You look very... nervous right now.
[chuckles]

00:14:46.093 --> 00:14:47.428
-Do I?
-Why are you nervous?

00:14:47.511 --> 00:14:48.387
I'm not nervous.

00:14:48.971 --> 00:14:49.847
I just, like...

00:14:56.729 --> 00:14:57.730
You are trouble,

00:14:57.813 --> 00:15:00.608
-and I can sense that you're trouble.
-There's nothing wrong with that.

00:15:00.691 --> 00:15:02.651
Sometimes if you can't be good,
you can be good at it.

00:15:02.735 --> 00:15:04.236
-Right.
-Be good at it.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.696
I'm good at lots of things.

00:15:05.779 --> 00:15:08.198
I hate you so much
in this moment right now.

00:15:08.282 --> 00:15:09.116
-Why?
-Because--

00:15:09.199 --> 00:15:11.201
-Because you're vulnerable?
-I see what you're doing.

00:15:11.285 --> 00:15:13.329
-I'm not doing anything.
-I pick up what you're putting down.

00:15:13.412 --> 00:15:14.496
What am I putting down?

00:15:15.873 --> 00:15:16.707
Funny.

00:15:19.835 --> 00:15:21.045
Terrible human being.

00:15:21.128 --> 00:15:22.171
What am I doing?

00:15:22.254 --> 00:15:23.505
What are you doing right now?

00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:25.758
I'm just trying to make a connection
with someone.

00:15:25.841 --> 00:15:29.178
I hate you so much. You're... [chuckles]

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:31.096
You're trouble.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.348
-I'm not.
-And you know you're trouble.

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:34.558
-I'm not trouble.
-You know you're trouble.

00:15:53.285 --> 00:15:54.370
[Brandon] Was that too hard?

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:57.873
Yes.
The most difficult thing I'll do in 2019.

00:15:57.957 --> 00:15:59.959
I... I hate you so much.

00:16:12.888 --> 00:16:13.722
Trouble.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.557
Big trouble.

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:17.351
You wanna go get a drink?

00:16:17.434 --> 00:16:18.394
Yeah, let's go.

00:16:19.228 --> 00:16:20.062
But see?

00:16:20.145 --> 00:16:22.481
If you just stop talking
for a few minutes, it wouldn't be so bad.

00:16:22.564 --> 00:16:23.983
If I just stop talking?

00:16:29.279 --> 00:16:31.281
[indistinct chatter]

00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:39.623
-This is really nice, huh?
-It's really beautiful. Yeah.

00:16:39.707 --> 00:16:42.042
-Kind of like Gone with the Wind fabulous.
-[laughs]

00:16:42.126 --> 00:16:43.252
Yeah.

00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:46.505
Actually, grab a couple drinks,
be right back?

00:16:46.588 --> 00:16:48.549
-Yeah, nice.
-Yeah? One second.

00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:57.016
There you go, sir.

00:16:57.141 --> 00:16:59.226
-Oh, nice, yeah.
-Very nice. Very nice.

00:16:59.727 --> 00:17:00.561
Come around this way.

00:17:00.644 --> 00:17:02.146
-I'll try not to spill it.
-I'll wait for you to sit.

00:17:02.229 --> 00:17:04.148
Look at you,
that's alcohol abuse right there.

00:17:04.231 --> 00:17:05.941
-Look at you!
-I can't help it, it's a mess.

00:17:06.024 --> 00:17:06.900
What's wrong with you?

00:17:06.984 --> 00:17:08.193
-Cheers.
-All right, cheers.

00:17:08.277 --> 00:17:10.237
-That is a very, very high pour.
-Mmm.

00:17:11.113 --> 00:17:14.950
And someone who can complement you...

00:17:15.033 --> 00:17:16.076
Mm-hmm.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.870
...bring something, a little spice.

00:17:17.953 --> 00:17:18.787
Yes.

00:17:19.121 --> 00:17:20.539
A good Cajun boy. [chuckles]

00:17:20.622 --> 00:17:22.416
I-- I think a good Cajun boy

00:17:22.916 --> 00:17:24.668
-could do that.
-I have a few friends.

00:17:24.752 --> 00:17:28.088
Okay. Can you introduce me? [laughs]

00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:30.591
All right, that's cool. No big deal.

00:17:32.468 --> 00:17:34.720
-I'm just making fun.
-No, that's cool.

00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:38.182
So do you feel like
whenever you find that relationship,

00:17:38.265 --> 00:17:40.476
do you think that you
lose a part of yourself or no?

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:41.435
[Brandon] Mm-mm.

00:17:41.769 --> 00:17:44.271
I've lost a part of myself
in, like, past relationships.

00:17:45.439 --> 00:17:48.150
And I've found, like,
what makes me happy again,

00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:50.402
and I feel like I'm at a good point
in my life now

00:17:50.486 --> 00:17:52.863
-where, like, I won't lose that again.
-Yeah.

00:17:52.946 --> 00:17:54.948
Like, it's a part of me.

00:17:55.032 --> 00:17:56.450
-I get that.
-How about you?

00:17:56.533 --> 00:17:59.661
I get that.
Well, I have nothing to base that off of.

00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:01.455
-You've never been in a relationship?
-Mm-mm.

00:18:01.538 --> 00:18:02.372
Ever?

00:18:02.456 --> 00:18:04.374
-Relationships are terrifying.
-Mm-hmm.

00:18:04.458 --> 00:18:07.127
And I think people get bored,
people get complacent and those things,

00:18:07.211 --> 00:18:08.921
and they lose sight of themselves.

00:18:09.421 --> 00:18:10.255
And, um...

00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:12.466
From my experience.

00:18:12.633 --> 00:18:15.177
[Brandon] You don't have any experience,
so how do you know?

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.429
I have no experience
of my own relationships.

00:18:17.513 --> 00:18:19.890
Just other people? People-watching?

00:18:19.973 --> 00:18:21.308
No, not even people-watching.

00:18:21.391 --> 00:18:24.061
I have first-hand experience
in other people's relationships.

00:18:24.895 --> 00:18:26.855
-That sounds like a good story.
-From my younger days.

00:18:26.939 --> 00:18:29.316
-Okay. Yes.
-Yeah, we won't... From my younger days.

00:18:31.151 --> 00:18:32.402
So do you want another?

00:18:32.736 --> 00:18:34.738
-I think I'm good with one.
-Okay, all right.

00:18:34.822 --> 00:18:37.241
-Perfect.
-One after-dinner drink is enough.

00:18:37.324 --> 00:18:39.201
-Perfect.
-I'll wait till you finish drinking yours.

00:18:39.284 --> 00:18:41.036
Um, then we might be here for a minute.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.163
-I'm actually enjoying the company, so...
-You're going slow?

00:18:43.247 --> 00:18:44.540
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:18:44.623 --> 00:18:46.834
You don't have to rush through everything.
 Just kinda...

00:18:48.752 --> 00:18:50.003
You're really cute.

00:18:50.087 --> 00:18:51.588
[Justin] You're really cute, too.

00:18:51.672 --> 00:18:53.340
-You think so?
-I do think so.

00:18:53.423 --> 00:18:54.508
-I'm glad you do.
-[chuckles]

00:18:54.591 --> 00:18:56.510
-I had a really good time tonight.
-Yeah?

00:18:56.969 --> 00:18:58.303
Yeah, you know...

00:18:58.387 --> 00:19:00.013
[laughs]

00:19:00.848 --> 00:19:01.974
Look at those palms.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.561
Like, dark lines.
Mine are, like, very light.

00:19:07.646 --> 00:19:10.190
-Lots of things fit together, I see.
-[chuckles] Yeah.

00:19:11.525 --> 00:19:12.359
So,

00:19:12.734 --> 00:19:14.862
you asked me earlier, um...

00:19:15.487 --> 00:19:16.989
-where I live.
-Yeah.

00:19:17.072 --> 00:19:19.741
And I live in Lower Garden District,
but...

00:19:20.826 --> 00:19:23.203
Very recently, I got a job in Austin.

00:19:23.287 --> 00:19:24.163
Nice.

00:19:24.246 --> 00:19:26.081
-So...
-That's awesome. Congrats for you.

00:19:26.165 --> 00:19:27.499
-Yeah.
-[glass clinks]

00:19:27.583 --> 00:19:28.750
When are you moving?

00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:29.960
-Soon.
-Yeah?

00:19:30.043 --> 00:19:30.919
Tomorrow?

00:19:31.169 --> 00:19:32.546
-Soonish.
-Like, after this?

00:19:32.629 --> 00:19:33.505
[laughs]

00:19:33.589 --> 00:19:34.840
Do you need me to help you pack?

00:19:34.923 --> 00:19:35.924
You're gonna help me pack?

00:19:36.008 --> 00:19:37.426
I like to organize.

00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:38.635
[chuckles]

00:19:38.719 --> 00:19:40.470
-You ready to go?
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:19:40.554 --> 00:19:42.181
-You want to walk downstairs?
-Sure.

00:19:42.264 --> 00:19:44.474
Let me put these back for us,
before I spill the rest.

00:19:44.558 --> 00:19:45.809
'Cause you'll probably spill it.

00:19:45.893 --> 00:19:47.477
Yeah, exactly. I'll do my best.

00:19:51.064 --> 00:19:53.066
-[Brandon] Are you ready?
-Yeah, let's go.

00:20:04.411 --> 00:20:05.495
You dropping me off?

00:20:05.913 --> 00:20:07.206
Yeah, you know.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:08.999
That's how I roll.

00:20:09.541 --> 00:20:10.751
I appreciate that.

00:20:13.253 --> 00:20:15.047
-Thank you.
-I like your beard.

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:15.964
Thank you.

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:17.507
Yeah, it's a little red.

00:20:17.591 --> 00:20:19.635
-It's a little red.
-You got a little ginger in you?

00:20:19.718 --> 00:20:20.552
Yeah, I do.

00:20:21.136 --> 00:20:22.095
Do this again?

00:20:22.846 --> 00:20:23.805
I hope so.

00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:24.848
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

00:20:24.932 --> 00:20:25.766
Okay.

00:20:25.849 --> 00:20:28.143
Do you wanna get my number,
should I get your number?

00:20:28.226 --> 00:20:29.478
-Yeah.
-Do you have your phone?

00:20:29.561 --> 00:20:30.646
Yeah.

00:20:31.855 --> 00:20:34.650
Your hand's getting dangerously close
to my inner thigh.

00:20:34.733 --> 00:20:35.734
-[laughs]
-I mean...

00:20:36.735 --> 00:20:39.446
I like when you get nervous,
what it does to your laugh.

00:20:39.529 --> 00:20:41.490
That's my normal generic laugh.

00:20:41.573 --> 00:20:44.034
-It's not a nervous laugh.
-I know, but it's a really good laugh.

00:20:44.117 --> 00:20:46.119
[laughs]

00:20:47.537 --> 00:20:48.455
So...

00:20:48.872 --> 00:20:49.915
Oh, God.

00:20:49.998 --> 00:20:53.210
When you were like,
"I'm moving to Austin," I'm like, "Oh...

00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:55.295
-This is what's wrong with him."
-I'm sorry.

00:20:55.379 --> 00:20:57.089
-[groans]
-This is what's wrong.

00:20:57.172 --> 00:21:00.425
Why does everything have to be...
Why does it have to be so complicated?

00:21:00.509 --> 00:21:02.469
Why can't it just be so easy?

00:21:02.552 --> 00:21:03.595
All right, Lauryn Hill.

00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:06.181
-I'm sorry.
-It's fine. It's not your fault.

00:21:06.264 --> 00:21:09.643
I was happy for you that you're moving
to Austin and you're doing...

00:21:09.726 --> 00:21:10.769
big boss stuff.

00:21:12.604 --> 00:21:15.190
-I'll be stuck in New Orleans, and...
-[chuckles]

00:21:19.778 --> 00:21:20.612
Why...

00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:23.448
So why do you do it?

00:21:25.617 --> 00:21:26.952
[Brandon] And this is your stop.

00:21:27.035 --> 00:21:29.621
All right, so, on that note... [laughs]

00:21:30.539 --> 00:21:32.082
-Thank you.
-Yeah, definitely.

00:21:32.165 --> 00:21:33.292
Can we do this again soon?

00:21:33.375 --> 00:21:34.209
I hope so.

00:21:34.459 --> 00:21:36.461
-Text me.
-Yeah, for sure.

00:21:43.176 --> 00:21:44.386
